{"Title":"An Act to increase safety on public ways","BillNumber":"H3299","DocketNumber":"HD4053","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"MSD1","Name":"Michael S. Day","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MSD1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T16:39:33.957"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"MSD1","Name":"Michael S. Day","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MSD1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T16:39:33.9566667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3299/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Day of Stoneham, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3299) of Michael S. Day relative to the towing of motor vehicles under operation by incapacitated persons.  Transportation.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1: General Laws Part I Title XVI Chapter 111E, is amended to include the following Section 9B which provides:\r\n\t(a)\t For the purposes of this section, “incapacitated” shall have the same meaning as is defined in Section 9A of Chapter 111E.\r\n\t(b)\tWhere an incapacitated person is found to be the operator of or in possession of a motor vehicle on a public way, that motor vehicle shall be towed away and impounded for a period of twelve (12) hours.\r\n\t(c)\tThis (12) hour impoundment period shall be calculated from the time the vehicle is towed. The costs for the towing, storage and maintenance of the vehicle shall be borne by the operator or individual who retrieves the vehicle after the twelve (12) hour hold period is complete.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J27","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Place in OD","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H52","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H52"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}